    <details class="insights-panel space-y-4"><summary class="insights-link">Definitions, coverage, and limitations</summary><div class="insights-muted space-y-3 text-sm"><p>{{ TutorInsightsReadModel::PROVIDER_BASIS }}</p><p>Suspension or withdrawal does not erase retained teaching history. Erased/deleted accounts and unresolved merged-away ownership are excluded. Unlinked appointments do not establish a person; the average uses linked appointments only.</p><p>Full valid stored UTC intervals are assigned to scheduled start, across midnight and DST. Invalid intervals remain in completed counts; their duration is unavailable or excluded from a labeled partial subtotal. Distinct overlapping bookings remain distinct; no live attendance or unique working time is inferred.</p><p>Operational cancellations use policy-decision records, reschedules use canonical reschedule rows, and LMS reviews use the latest explicit final-review date. Overwritten review history and ordinary homework review history cannot be reconstructed. Audit/notification mirrors are not counted.</p><p>Feedback includes currently available conversations, administrator message events, and actual transitions into resolved. Reopening then resolving again creates another transition. Erased or currently inaccessible feedback is excluded; subjects, bodies, context contents and read states are never used.</p><p>Coverage is unknown before retained records. Zero means no recorded qualifying activity. Source queries share one generation instant but do not claim database snapshot isolation. Definition: {{ TutorInsightsContext::VERSION }}.</p></div></details>
